Under CC BY 4.0, licensees must provide appropriate attribution, reference
this license, and indicate whether licensed material was modified. The license
permits reuse, sharing and adaptation, including for commercial purposes.
There are no restrictions to non-commercial research only.

EXCLUDED MATERIAL AND THIRD-PARTY RIGHTS

This CC BY 4.0 notice does NOT license:
  - software source files in code/ or scripts/ (software licensing is pending);
  - MATLAB, EIDORS and other third-party programs and dependencies;
  - files explicitly identified as third-party works or carrying separate
    rights, if any. Rights can only be granted by their lawful owners.

Publishing the source code for inspection does not, by itself, authorize
others to modify or redistribute it. The authors should approve a software
license separately (for example, MIT) after confirming code ownership and
compatibility with third-party obligations. No such approval is assumed here.

This notice is intended to apply CC BY 4.0 to the above-listed author-owned
research data and documentation only. Check contributor/organization rights
and remove any third-party materials that cannot be licensed before release.
